  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B047",
        "laureates": [
          "Jens Juul Holst",
          "Svetlana Mojsov",
          "Daniel J. Drucker"
        ],
        "citation": "for discoveries of GLP-1 physiology that enabled transformative therapies for diabetes and obesity"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B041",
    "B029"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "I retain B047 and the Holst-Mojsov-Drucker configuration. On the supplied record, it is an unusually mature achievement that links a defined physiological system to established, major therapeutic benefit in diabetes and obesity. The citation is deliberately limited to discoveries of GLP-1 physiology and their enabling role, rather than claiming credit for all subsequent drug optimization. The proposed trio remains a coherent representation of hormone physiology, peptide biology, and translation.",
    "case_against": "Attribution remains the principal weakness. Lotte Bjerre Knudsen is also listed among the credited names, and the evidence does not fully settle whether a three-person award can fairly separate foundational GLP-1 work from essential medicinal optimization and industrial development. This reservation is material, even though it does not on balance displace B047.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "sandberg-rickard",
        "point": "Sandberg prefers B029 because the unfolded protein response is a mature fundamental mechanism with a compact Mori-Walter attribution, whereas B047 has a more difficult allocation among foundational biology and therapeutic development.",
        "response": "I agree that B029 has a particularly strong claim in mechanistic clarity, maturity, and concise credit. The common comparison should not require immediate clinical application of every foundational discovery. Nonetheless, the supplied evidence for B047 demonstrates both fundamental physiological significance and a direct, durable transformation of treatment across two major diseases. A narrowly limited citation preserves that scientific core; B029 remains my leading foundational-science alternative."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "svenningsson-per",
        "point": "Svenningsson prefers B041 for its mature prevention of HPV infection and related cancers, while arguing that its achievement and attribution may be more delimited than those of B047.",
        "response": "B041 is an exceptional alternative and its preventive medical consequence is at least as relevant to common criteria as therapeutic impact. But its supplied record still leaves unresolved divisions among papillomavirus biology, VLP work, vaccine development, and translation. B047 has a similarly demanding attribution question, yet its proposed trio and physiology-focused citation give a sufficiently intelligible allocation on the present evidence. I therefore retain B047 rather than treating either candidate's broader support as dispositive."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
        "point": "Wahren-Herlenius prefers B023 because the discovery of distinct B- and T-lymphocyte lineages is an enduring foundational principle with complementary two-person attribution.",
        "response": "B023 illustrates the value of rewarding a foundational, long-confirmed conceptual advance even when its medical effects are mediated through later work. Its concise formulation is a real comparative advantage. I still judge B047 stronger under the same criteria because it combines a foundational physiological discovery, decades of maturity, and direct established benefit, while keeping the cited achievement narrow enough to avoid absorbing the larger subsequent therapeutic enterprise."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the historical record can justify excluding Lotte Bjerre Knudsen from the proposed three-person allocation while fairly distinguishing foundational GLP-1 discovery from later therapeutic development.",
      "Whether the supplied evidence permits sufficiently precise attribution among the three proposed B041 laureates to make that candidate preferable to B047.",
      "How finely a final citation must distinguish enabling GLP-1 physiology from later drug optimization."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No documented conflict is apparent from the supplied profile. My recorded co-authorship connections do not include any proposed laureate or other named contributor in the preferred configuration."
  }
}
